  - After a successful login, the submit handler calls [38;5;153msession.setCurrentUser(...)[39m. Writing the session is the caller's
    job, not [38;5;153mlogin()[39m's. That keeps [38;5;153mlogin()[39m a pure "verify credentials" call.
  - It gains [38;5;153mimport { session } from './session.js'[39m.

  [1m[38;5;153mindex.html[39m:[0m [38;5;153m<script src="app.js">[39m becomes [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m.

  [1mNot included (YAGNI):[0m a logout button or UI. [38;5;153mclearCurrentUser()[39m exists for when one is added. Also not included: login
  history and any server-side session.

